  "id": "lateralization",
  "term": "lateralization",
  "definition": "Lateralization is the tendency for some brain functions or mental processes to be handled more by one cerebral hemisphere than the other. In cognition, this means that certain activities, such as language or spatial processing, rely more strongly on the left or right side of the brain.",
